  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-18T16:42:30.469Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Is it possible that a social networking service shows that your friends are in a group instance, but you can't actually join that instance?\n\n・Unable to access a group-only instance created within a group I'm already a member of (403 error)\n\n・Social features allow you to see if your friends are in that instance.\n\n・Within that group, no roles other than the group owner have been created (anyone who is in the group should be able to join).\n\n・In group activity, the group instance will not be displayed(The same behavior occurs on websites.).\n\n・I cannot create a group instance from my end.\n\n・Sometimes I can add someone to a group instance, and sometimes I can't (the reason is unknown, and it's not reproducible).\n\n・Clearing the cache, logging out and logging back in, and restarting the PC did not fix the problem.\n\nBased on these factors, it appears that there are permission issues within the group.\n\nI've been struggling with this for two years now; it's only happening in one group, and although I've reported it before, it still hasn't been fixed.\n\nPlease do something about it.",
